1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,990
Stare at red, then look at a white wall…

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:06,010
Mix the three lights and you get white

3
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:08,180
Stare at the dot in the middle
of the red circle for 15 seconds

4
00:00:08,230 --> 00:00:11,050
Then look at a white screen…

5
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:19,820
Don't take your eyes off the center dot

6
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:27,800
Just a little longer!

7
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:29,900
What do you see?

8
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:34,720
A cyan circle appears!

9
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:36,820
Your eye has three kinds
of color-sensing cells

10
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:40,257
Stare at red for a long time
and only the red cells keep working

11
00:00:40,307 --> 00:00:42,727
White light = red + green + blue
but the red cells are tired…

12
00:00:42,777 --> 00:00:47,497
Only green + blue are left,
so you see cyan!

13
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:52,867
Other colors show their opposite color too

14
00:00:52,917 --> 00:00:55,117
After a short rest the cells recover
and it fades away

15
00:00:55,167 --> 00:00:58,717
NEXT: Why is summer hot?
